### 5. Route Registration
```javascript
// src/router/index.jsx
import React, { lazy, Suspense } from 'react'
import { Routes, Route } from 'react-router-dom'
import { Box, CircularProgress } from '@mui/material'

// Lazy load pages
const ConversationsPage = lazy(() => import('pages/ConversationsPage'))
const MusicRoomPage = lazy(() => import('pages/MusicRoomPage'))
const ProfilePage = lazy(() => import('pages/ProfilePage'))
const LoginPage = lazy(() => import('pages/LoginPage'))

const PageLoader = () => (
  <Box display="flex" justifyContent="center" alignItems="center" minHeight="400px">
    <CircularProgress />
  </Box>
)

const AppRouter = () => {
  return (
    <Suspense fallback={<PageLoader />}>
      <Routes>
        <Route path="/login" element={<LoginPage />} />
        <Route path="/conversations" element={<ConversationsPage />} />
        <Route path="/rooms/:roomId" element={<MusicRoomPage />} />
        <Route path="/profile" element={<ProfilePage />} />
      </Routes>
    </Suspense>
  )
}

export default AppRouter
```

React Router v7 (`^7.18.1`) is installed — the `Routes`/`Route`/`lazy` pattern
above is the current data-router-agnostic style; if the project later adopts
v7's `createBrowserRouter`/loader-based routing, update this template
accordingly rather than mixing both styles.

### 6. Page Requirements Checklist

#### ✅ Page Component
- [ ] Minimal component that delegates to a container
- [ ] Single responsibility: route rendering
- [ ] No business logic or state management
- [ ] Use absolute imports once the alias is configured (not set up yet —
      see the architecture rules)

#### ✅ Container Component
- [ ] Lives under `src/features/containers/<domain>/`, not a top-level
      `containers/` folder
- [ ] Contains all business logic
- [ ] Manages state and API calls
- [ ] Handles user interactions
- [ ] Renders reusable components from `src/components/<domain>/`
- [ ] Uses RTK Query for API calls
- [ ] Uses Redux slices for client-owned state only (not server-response
      caching — see the state-layer rules)

#### ✅ Route Integration
- [ ] Register route in `src/router/index.jsx`
- [ ] Use lazy loading for performance
- [ ] Add proper loading states
- [ ] Include error boundaries

#### ✅ Rhynk Specific
- [ ] Include proper error handling for API/socket failures
- [ ] Add loading states for API calls
- [ ] Include mobile responsiveness with MUI breakpoints
- [ ] Use MUI SX prop for all styling
- [ ] For music-room pages, don't build mid-session provider hot-swap or
      derive playback position from anything but server sync broadcasts
      (see [[08-music-rooms]])

### 7. Common Page Patterns

#### List Pages (Conversations, Notifications)
- Display data in lists or cards
- Include search and filter functionality
- Add pagination/cursor-based infinite scroll for large datasets

#### Form Pages (Login, Register, OTP Verification)
- Multi-step flows with validation
- Progress indicators
- Clear error messaging mapped to server error codes

#### Detail Pages (Music Room, Conversation Thread)
- Display comprehensive real-time state
- Include related actions (DJ controls, message composer)
- Include navigation back to the list

#### Dashboard-style Pages (Profile, Notifications)
- Summary cards with key info
- Quick action buttons
- Real-time data updates via sockets once wired up

### 8. Testing

No test runner (Vitest/Jest) is configured in this repo yet — the template
below is the intended shape once one is added, not something that runs today.

```javascript
// src/pages/__tests__/ConversationsPage.test.jsx
import React from 'react'
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react'
import { Provider } from 'react-redux'
import { BrowserRouter } from 'react-router-dom'
import { configureStore } from '@reduxjs/toolkit'
import ConversationsPage from '../ConversationsPage'

const createTestStore = () => {
  return configureStore({
    reducer: {
      presence: (state = { activeConversationId: null }, action) => state
    }
  })
}

const TestWrapper = ({ children }) => {
  const store = createTestStore()

  return (
    <Provider store={store}>
      <BrowserRouter>
        {children}
      </BrowserRouter>
    </Provider>
  )
}

describe('ConversationsPage', () => {
  it('renders without crashing', () => {
    render(
      <TestWrapper>
        <ConversationsPage />
      </TestWrapper>
    )

    expect(screen.getByText('Conversations')).toBeInTheDocument()
  })
})
```
